        hardEdges: ["Don't reduce this to 'religion vs. secularism.' Augustine is saying politics is always theological — always shaped by what the society loves most. The question is which love, not whether love is involved.", "Augustine wrote this after the fall of Rome. He is not abstract — he is watching an empire collapse and asking why."],
