        dinnerQuestion: "Why is there something rather than nothing — and is 'we don't know' a better answer than 'God'?",
        transfer: [{ label: "Science", note: "The Third Way (contingency) is the cosmological argument — why is there something rather than nothing? Physics addresses mechanism, not ground." }, { label: "Greeks", note: "The First Way (motion) is Aristotle's unmoved mover in Christian dress. Aquinas baptized Aristotle." }],
